  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "status": "resolved",
      "detail": "Serialized transcript growth now reserves worst-case JSON escaped next pair under 1MB before spending request or mutating transcript; escaped quota and request serialization failures return typed errors and preserve state."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "status": "resolved",
      "detail": "Configure revokes enablement and cancels pending transport before validating replacement path. New and Select also cancel before quota/identity errors; capacity cancellation test passed."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "status": "resolved",
      "detail": "Retry is derived exclusively from selected session last failed user entry; another chat cannot recover prior failed message via global retry state. Source reviewed; independent Qt review covers interaction."
    },
    {
      "severity": "informational",
      "status": "reviewed",
      "detail": "New host-only chat.1 service has no registry/kernel handles or execution operations. Host owns roles, fixed system text, bounded completed-pair context and session routing. Text is inserted inertly; external links disabled. Accepted credential and HTTPS transport sources are reused unchanged. Session opt-in, explicit sends, one pending exchange, timeout, cancellation/reaping and Qt token fences remain in place."
    },
    {
      "severity": "informational",
      "status": "reviewed",
      "detail": "Strict empty-struct protocol variants reject unknown New/Cancel/Quit fields. Independent real-process invalid duplicate/unknown/oversized frame tests, disabled production startup and fixture-isolated multiturn/cancel passed. Production binary rejects fixture flag."
    },
    {
      "severity": "informational",
      "status": "reviewed",
      "detail": "Independent final native suite16/16, process suite3/3, fmt, clippy and accepted-source preservation passed without ignored/skipped tests. No actual key was read or inference initiated. The user-authorized contextual-chat pivot is a separate trust/protocol scope from archived UX001, not an extension of its approval."
    }
  ],
